{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>I loved</b> — How I would love that HaShem hear my voice when I plead. And some say:" "<b>I loved YHWH, for He hears the voice of my supplications</b> — like: 'which the wise will declare and not conceal' [Job 15:18]." "And some say: that the yod in קולי is superfluous. And the correct interpretation: that the bet is missing from תחנוני [i.e., it should be read as בתחנוני]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:47.309121384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}